Individual model vulnerabilities vary dramatically across the attack taxonomy (Figure~\ref{fig:per_model_asr}). Content-dependent attacks (prompt injection, sycophancy) exploit capability gaps, producing strong ASR--capability correlations ($r{>}0.7$). Structural attacks (position bias) show uniformly moderate ASR regardless of model capability, consistent with their mechanism operating on presentation order rather than response content.

