The distributional analysis (Figure~\ref{fig:asr_distribution}) reveals that larger panels compress ASR variance without eliminating it: at $K{=}7$, the interquartile range remains 0.05--0.15 for most attacks. This residual variance is the signal that $K_{\mathrm{eff}}$ and $\eta_{\max}$ predict in the regression framework.

\subsection{Pairwise Mutual Information Structure}
\label{app:mi_structure}

